VOT Stimuli
===========

This directory contains the audio stimuli generated using a modified
version of Matthew Winn's Praat script. The resulting WAV files were
used in the experiements conducted for this paper.

The stimuli consist of a seven-step deer-tier continuum with target
VOT values ranging from 10 to 70ms in 10ms increments. Resampled copies
were made at 16khz for use with HuBERT.

The original implementation used (version 30) and accompanying materials
are available from the University of Minnesota repository:

	https://github.com/ListenLab/VOT.git


MODIFICATIONS
-------------

	The original script was modified to generate a seven-step
	VOT continuum using a unified F0 level.

	Covariance of aspiration-intensity was disabled, and the
	interpolation procedure was corrected to handle single-step
	F0 generation.

REFERENCE
---------

	Matthew B. Winn; Manipulation of voice onset time in speech stimuli: A tutorial and flexible Praat script. J. Acoust. Soc. Am. 1 February 2020; 147 (2): 852–866. 
	https://doi.org/10.1121/10.0000692

